<!--
  AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 (xhigh effort) via Claude Code, 2026-10-10: wrote the URDF/xacro, launch file and tests.
  AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code, 2026-10-16: drew the plate's rounded front (front_slices, from the
  classmate's plate CAD in the private course repo (plate CAD is not published here)) and updated the plate comments for the CAD outline.

  beaconmind_car.urdf.xacro: the ONE robot description of Xiaohui Chen's two-wheel car, shared by
    (a) the Module 6 Gazebo Fortress lab (assignments/assignment6, wrapped with the instructor's <gazebo> blocks), and
    (b) the BeaconMind course project (robot_state_publisher TF tree, C12; Isaac Sim twin, M2.T4 / M2.T16).

  Frames (README C1): base_link = midpoint between the drive-wheel centres AT AXLE HEIGHT (z = 0 at the axle);
  +x toward the camera lens / caster end (the front); +y = robot left; +z up. Floor is at z = -wheel_radius.
  Every number comes from two files in this folder: car_props.xacro, GENERATED by beaconmind_description/gen_props.py
  from configs/car.json (M1.T9; never edit it by hand), and car_geometry_extras.xacro, hand-written, for the geometry
  car.json does not carry (plate outline, part boxes, part masses). Both label each value measured / derived /
  ESTIMATE / ASSUMED / stand-in. The camera pose stays provisional until configs/camera.json (M1.T7) exists.

  Links (exactly): base_link, chassis_link, left_wheel_link, right_wheel_link, caster_link, camera_link,
  camera_optical_frame, imu_link.
  This file has NO <gazebo>, <sensor>, ray or lidar elements (D1a: no range sensor). Simulator-specific
  blocks belong in a wrapper (for the lab: assignments/assignment6/lab-step10/gazebo_car.urdf.xacro).
-->
<robot name="beaconmind_car">
  <!-- ================= base_link: the axle midpoint (no visual, no inertia) ================= -->
  <!-- No <inertial> here on purpose: KDL (robot_state_publisher) does not support an inertia on the root link,
       so the body's mass lives in chassis_link, attached by a fixed joint.
       Isaac Sim (M2.T16): base_link and camera_optical_frame are the two links with NO <inertial> (no mass). How the
       Isaac URDF importer treats a massless link with merge_fixed_joints = False is NOT verified here. After the
       import, M2.T16 must check that neither became a rigid body with a default mass (the car's total must stay
       0.506 kg) and that the import log has no warnings about them. (In the Gazebo lab, sdformat's URDF converter
       merges fixed-joint links into their parent by default, so these frames get no body of their own there.) -->
  <link name="base_link"/>
  <!-- ================= chassis_link: the plate and everything rigidly on it ================= -->
